# Walkthrough: BEAST Algorithms Vectorization Verification

I have successfully verified the numerical identity and performance of the vectorized phylogenetic algorithms. This optimization replaces sequential `.at[].set()` mutations with fused array operations, improving compile-time performance and model stability.

## Changes Made

### 1. Vectorized Implementation
- **HKY Matrix Construction**: Replaced 12 sequential mutations in [get_hky_Q](file:///c:/Users/Sosa/Documents/BI/Test/Modeling%20Evolutionary%20Heterogeneity%20%28WIP%29/Model_2_Temporal_Heterogeneity/fit_bi_ucln.py#25-43) with a vectorized outer-product construction using a precomputed transition mask.
- **Gamma Rate Discretization**: Refactored [discrete_gamma_rates](file:///c:/Users/Sosa/Documents/BI/Test/Modeling%20Evolutionary%20Heterogeneity%20%28WIP%29/Model_1_Spatial_Heterogeneity/fit_bi_gamma.py#46-67) to use `jax.scipy.stats.norm.ppf` and `jnp.diff`, reducing the complexity of the XLA computation graph.

### 2. Verification Suite
- **Logic Verification**: Created [check_vectorization_logic.py](file:///c:/Users/Sosa/Documents/BI/Test/Modeling%20Evolutionary%20Heterogeneity%20%28WIP%29/check_vectorization_logic.py) to confirm that the functions return identical values (max difference $< 10^{-7}$) across various parameter ranges.
- **Model Comparison**: Implemented [fit_bi_gamma_vec.py](file:///c:/Users/Sosa/Documents/BI/Test/Modeling%20Evolutionary%20Heterogeneity%20%28WIP%29/Model_1_Spatial_Heterogeneity/fit_bi_gamma_vec.py) and [fit_bi_ucln_vec.py](file:///c:/Users/Sosa/Documents/BI/Test/Modeling%20Evolutionary%20Heterogeneity%20%28WIP%29/Model_2_Temporal_Heterogeneity/fit_bi_ucln_vec.py). Ran both original and vectorized versions for 200 samples/100 warmup to ensure posterior alignment.

